  (writeErrStr "fatal: systemstack called from unexpected goroutine"))



































(go/func ^:extern ^:go/noescape ^{:go/linkname "memclrNoHeapPointers"} memclrNoHeapPointers "memclrNoHeapPointers clears n bytes starting at ptr.\n\nUsually you should use typedmemclr. memclrNoHeapPointers should be\nused only when the caller knows that *ptr contains no heap pointers\nbecause either:\n\n*ptr is initialized memory and its type is pointer-free, or\n\n*ptr is uninitialized memory (e.g., memory that's being reused\nfor a new allocation) and hence contains only \"junk\".\n\nmemclrNoHeapPointers ensures that if ptr is pointer-aligned, and n\nis a multiple of the pointer size, then any pointer-aligned,\npointer-sized portion is cleared atomically. Despite the function\nname, this is necessary because this function is the underlying\nimplementation of typedmemclr and memclrHasPointers. See the doc of\nmemmove for more details.\n\nThe (CPU-specific) implementations of this function are in memclr_*.s.\n\nmemclrNoHeapPointers should be an internal detail,\nbut widely used packages access it using linkname.\nNotable members of the hall of shame include:\n  - github.com/bytedance/sonic\n  - github.com/chenzhuoyu/iasm\n  - github.com/dgraph-io/ristretto\n  - github.com/outcaste-io/ristretto\n\nDo not remove or change the type signature.\nSee go.dev/issue/67401.\n" [^unsafe/Pointer ptr ^uintptr n])


